REMINDER: Final JSON keys: "summary" (string), "pr_summary" (2-4 line summary of what the PR does — omit when unsure), "walkthrough" (array of {file_path, description} — one short entry per changed file you can describe from the diff, omit files you cannot describe), "change_diagram" (raw Mermaid, no fences — flowchart or sequence diagram of how the changed pieces connect, omit when too small to diagram or relationships are unclear), "comments" (array of {file_path,line_number,severity,message, plus optional suggested_code,suggestion_start_line,suggestion_end_line,original_lines for a small exact fix — omit all four when unsure}), "confidence_evaluations" (array), "investigation_complete" (bool), "loop_complete" (bool). No other top-level keys. No HTML in message strings. line_number is the "N | " annotation shown on the cited line (new-file line number) — never count lines yourself.
